  ('mahahual-mexico', '10S', 'Mahahual (Costa Maya & Banco Chinchorro)', 'Mexico', 'The largest coral atoll in the Northern Hemisphere', 'live', 'verified', 'oceanAerial', 'Quintana Roo (Cancún & Riviera Maya)', '{"liveaboard","diveglobal"}', '{}', '{"comfort","premier"}', null, 'anchor', '{"key_facts":["Banco Chinchorro - largest coral atoll in the Northern Hemisphere; biosphere 144,000 ha; ~25x10 mi","~80-90 min (some ops ~2.5h) boat from Mahahual; ~200 shipwrecks; permit-restricted (op handles permit)","Best viz May-Sep (~15-30m); crocodile-encounter season Jun 1-Sep 30 (XTC = sole federal permit)","Overnight = palafito stilt-hut on Cayo Centro (legalized 2010; no services) - the liveaboard-style product","Costa Maya cruise port (2nd-largest in Caribbean Mexico, up to ~20k cruisers) = OUT of TWW cruise scope"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","dan_emergency":"+1-919-684-9111","nearest_chamber":"Costamed, COZUMEL (DAN-certified) - Mahahual clinic has NO chamber; long medevac from Chinchorro","nearest_trauma":"Chetumal (Hospital General, south) or evac to Cancun","malaria":"NONE in tourist zone; dengue present","water":"bottled/purified","hurricane":"Jun-Nov, peak Aug-Oct","dive_no_fly":"18-24h (DAN)","special_rule":"REMOTE-MEDEVAC - dive conservative; permitted+certified op only; croc encounter handler-led, max 6/trip","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-20T14:49:02Z","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00","source_country":"mexico","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely","fcdo_zones":[{"name":"The city of Tijuana, in Baja California","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["airside transit through Tijuana airport","the Cross Border Xpress bridge linking the airport across the border","federal toll road 1D and the Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border"]},{"name":"The city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"The state of Chihuahua","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Chihuahua","the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez via federal toll road 45","federal toll road 45D between Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez","the Copper Canyon rail route and the towns immediately on it, including Creel","the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro","state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua"],"note":"The advisory also covers the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"name":"The state of Sinaloa","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán","road 32 between El Fuerte and Los Mochis","the 15D federal toll road running the length of the state","the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis and El Fuerte, and the towns immediately on it"]},{"name":"The state of Tamaulipas","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo via federal toll road 85D from Monterrey","federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad Victoria and Magueyes","the area of Tamaulipas south of those highways"]},{"name":"The state of Zacatecas","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"In Guanajuato: the areas south-west of road 45D","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D. (San Miguel de Allende and Guanajuato City sit outside this area.)"},{"name":"The state of Michoacán","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Morelia via federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43","toll road 48D between Morelia and its airport","the town of Pátzcuaro via toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips on Lake Pátzcuaro","Federal Highway 15D"]},{"name":"In Jalisco: the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the Colima border","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Thirty-nine named municipalities, including Autlán de Navarro, Sayula, Tapalpa, Cocula and Villa Corona — the advisory lists each by name."},{"name":"In Jalisco: eleven northern municipalities","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Bolaños, Chimaltitán, Colotlán, Hostotipaquillo, Huejúcar, Huequilla el Alto, Mezquitic, San Martín de Bolaños, Santa María de los Ángeles, Totatiche and Villa Guerrero."},{"name":"The state of Colima","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Manzanillo by sea, or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport","direct travel via road 200 from that airport to Manzanillo"]},{"name":"The state of Guerrero, including the city of Acapulco","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air"]},{"name":"Within 40km of the Guatemalan border, from the Pacific Coast up to and including the Gracias a Dios crossing","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"Federal Highway 199 between Rancho Nuevo, outside San Cristóbal de las Casas, and the Chancalá junction outside Palenque","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"The restriction is the highway segment, not the towns at either end."}],"fcdo_zones_provenance":{"file":"src/data/safety.json","ref":"f8666636bc25790e0c9643ad5656f8d9fea37bf6","ref_committed":"2026-08-30T05:44:55Z","country_iso2":"MX","summary":"The FCDO advises against all but essential travel to named states, cities and border areas of Mexico — listed below in its own words, each with its own exceptions. The Yucatán Peninsula, Mexico City, Baja California Sur and the other main visitor regions carry no FCDO restriction.","source":"UK FCDO — Mexico travel advice, reviewed 2026-07-16 (verbatim snapshot from the research library)","_rule":"the FCDO restricted-area records for this country, verbatim. PRESENCE OF THIS BLOCK IS NOT A CLAIM THAT THIS DESTINATION SITS IN ANY OF THEM — membership is a coverage judgement and is set only in `zone_record`, by a human."},"dive_emergency_numbers_verified":{"read":"2026-08-30","numbers":{"+1-919-684-9111":"DAN 24/7 emergency hotline — dan.org/about-dan/contact/, read 2026-08-30"},"_rule":"Each number above was read from the authority named beside it on the date shown. ⛔ A number with no entry here has NOT been verified and must not be presented as an emergency contact."}},"timing":{"peak":"Dive peak May-Sep (viz ~15-30m; croc encounter hard window Jun 1-Sep 30)","shoulder":"Apr and Oct edges","green":"Nov-Mar (wind/swell; Chinchorro often blown out - fall back to Costa Maya/Xcalak reef)","booking_lead":"4-6 months for permit-limited summer Chinchorro/croc product (permit scarcity = longer lead than a general reef trip)","off_season_specials":"winter Nov-Mar: Costa Maya/Xcalak mainland-reef dive days + no-fly beach fill-the-beds (lean Xcalak, south of the cruise port)","event_peaks":"croc window Jun 1-Sep 30; (Costa Maya cruise day-crowds peak Sep-Dec, busiest Nov, Wed/Thu - OUT of TWW scope, plan dive departures around it)","fire_date":"live by Dec-Jan, ~4-6 months ahead of the May-Sep dive window; run a winter Xcalak-reef value campaign for Nov-Mar fill-the-beds"},"jewels":[{"name":"Chinchorro overnight palafito expedition (Cayo Centro)","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards","status":"live","bookable_category":"multi-day dive expedition","tier":"premier","source":"https://pepedivemahahual.com/en/diving/chinchorro/","timing":"Dive peak May-Sep","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"multi-day dive with stilt-hut overnight on the atoll ·","si":"liveaboard","blurb":"multi-day dive with stilt-hut overnight on the atoll ·","when":"Dive peak May-Sep","commission":"on application (liveaboard-reseller/dive-op host)","wells":["stay","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["diveglobal","liveaboard"],"shelf_fit":{"diveglobal":"evidenced","liveaboard":"primary"},"commission_lane":["operator"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"~200-wreck atoll dives","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards","status":"live","bookable_category":"wreck/wall diving","tier":"premier","source":"https://xtcdivecenter.com/chinchorro/","timing":"Dive peak May-Sep","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","when":"Dive peak May-Sep","commission":"dive-op host ~10-20% / on application","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["diveglobal","liveaboard"],"shelf_fit":{"diveglobal":"evidenced","liveaboard":"primary"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":20,"commission_lane":["operator"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Chinchorro day-boat 2-3 tank + Cayo Centro","si_tag":"Dive Globally","status":"live","bookable_category":"day dive charter","tier":"comfort","source":"https://xtcdivecenter.com/chinchorro/","timing":"Dive peak May-Sep","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"state day-trip, 2-tank $275 / 3-tank $325, Cayo Centro surface stop ·","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"state day-trip, 2-tank $275 / 3-tank $325, Cayo Centro surface stop ·","when":"Dive peak May-Sep","commission":"dive-op host / affiliate","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["diveglobal","liveaboard"],"shelf_fit":{"diveglobal":"primary","liveaboard":"evidenced"},"commission_lane":["operator","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Costa Maya / Xcalak reef diving","si_tag":"Dive Globally","status":"live","bookable_category":"day dive charter","tier":"comfort","source":"https://amigosdelmar.net/","timing":"Dive peak May-Sep","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"diveglobal","when":"Dive peak May-Sep","commission":"dive-op host ~10-20%","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["diveglobal"],"shelf_fit":{"diveglobal":"primary","liveaboard":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":20,"commission_lane":["operator"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Wild American-crocodile in-water encounter (XTC)","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"future","bookable_category":"expert-guided wildlife","tier":"premier","source":"https://xtcdivecenter.com/crocs/croc-encounters/","timing":"Dive peak May-Sep","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"handler-led encounter, world''s only permitted such experience ·","si":"expedition","blurb":"handler-led encounter, world''s only permitted such experience ·","when":"Dive peak May-Sep","commission":"dive-op host / on application; XTC sole permit","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"diveglobal":"destination","expedition":"primary","liveaboard":"destination"},"commission_lane":["operator"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for diving Mahahual?","a":"Remote medevac - the load-bearing risk. Mahahual has NO hyperbaric chamber; the nearest DAN-certified chamber is in Cozumel, a multi-hour transit from a Chinchorro site ~25 miles offshore. Dive conservatively, hold no-fly 18-24h, and treat DCS as a logistics problem.","source":"costamed.com.mx","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"When is the best time to dive Mahahual and Chinchorro?","a":"May-September - the counterintuitive answer: calmest seas, best visibility (~15-30m) and the crocodile season (Jun 1-Sep 30), even though it overlaps the rainy/hurricane months. Winter (Nov-Mar) sees more wind and Chinchorro is often blown out.","source":"coralrealm.com","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Can I day-dive Banco Chinchorro, and how?","a":"Yes - most Mahahual/Xcalak operators run day-trips for certified divers: a 2-tank ($275) or 3-tank ($325) day with a Cayo Centro stop, an 80-90-minute crossing each way. The operator handles the limited federal permit when you book; May-September has the calmest seas.","source":"xtcdivecenter.com","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Can you really swim with wild crocodiles at Chinchorro?","a":"Yes - it''s the only legally permitted in-water wild-crocodile encounter on Earth, and only XTC Dive Center holds the federal permit. The season is a hard window of June 1 to September 30, capped at 6 people (2 in the water with the handler at a time), flotation device required. Book far ahead.","source":"xtcdivecenter.com","si_tag":"globaladv"},{"q":"What is the Banco Chinchorro liveaboard experience actually like?","a":"It''s a stilt-hut expedition, not a cruise ship. Multi-day trips overnight in a palafito on Cayo Centro - a basic 2x2m stilt-deck fishing hut with hammocks and no services - legalized in 2010. It''s the closest access to the remote walls and ~200 wrecks; permit-scarce, so book the specialist operator well ahead.","source":"pepedivemahahual.com","si_tag":"liveaboard"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Mahahual & Banco Chinchorro: Atoll Diving Guide","meta_description":"Mahahual is the gateway to Banco Chinchorro - the Northern Hemisphere''s largest coral atoll: ~200 wrecks, croc encounters, and the remote-chamber realities.","slug":"mahahual-mexico","primary_keyword":"Banco Chinchorro diving","long_tail":["Mahahual Banco Chinchorro dive","Chinchorro liveaboard palafito","Chinchorro crocodile snorkel XTC","Costa Maya diving","Xcalak scuba diving"],"search_language":"es","local_keywords":["buceo Banco Chinchorro","Mahahual buceo Costa Maya","encuentro con cocodrilos Xcalak","buceo Xcalak","atolon Chinchorro liveaboard palafito"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-04","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"