  ('manuel-antonio-costa-rica', '10S', 'Manuel Antonio', 'Costa Rica', 'Sloths, monkeys and Pacific cliffs', 'live', 'verified', 'tropicalBeach', 'Costa Rica', '{"tropical","expedition","wildlife"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Manuel Antonio NP is open Wed–Mon 07:00–16:00, CLOSED every Tuesday; adult entry US$18, child (2–12) US$5, under-2 free; advance online ticket + passport number required.","One of few places to see all of Costa Rica''s iconic wildlife at a beach: 2- & 3-toed sloths, white-faced capuchins (90%+ of visits), endangered Central American squirrel monkeys, howlers, coatis, toucans.","Two park beaches: crescent Playa Manuel Antonio (calm, turquoise — the calmest, patrolled swim) and longer, choppier Playa Espadilla Sur.","Access: ~2.5–3 hr / ~168 km drive from San José (SJO), OR ~25-min domestic flight to Quepos–Manuel Antonio (XQP) on Sansa / Costa Rica Green Airways + 15 km / 25-min transfer.","Cliffside-resort belt (Arenas del Mar, Makanda, Gaia, Tulemar) makes it a top romance/honeymoon hub; hillside villas make it a strong family/multi-gen hub."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"Hospital Metropolitano Quepos (private, 24-hr, marina) + public Max Terán Valls Hospital; serious cases to San José major hospitals (~2.5–3 hr) with air evac available","book_enabled":true,"l2_disclosure":true,"advisory_note":"standard caution — petty crime, don''t display wealth, avoid poorly lit beaches at night, enroll in STEP","air_access_verified":"SJO gateway; XQP (Quepos–Manuel Antonio) ~25-min domestic flight on Sansa / Costa Rica Green Airways, or ~2.5–3 hr drive from SJO","riptide":"HARD FLAG — rip currents are the leading cause of tourist drowning in Costa Rica (>80% of drownings); most beaches unguarded. Swim only at guarded/flagged beaches (the park cove is the calmest and patrolled), heed red flags, never swim alone; if caught, swim parallel to shore.","wildlife":"Bold habituated monkeys/raccoons/coatis raid food — no feeding, seal food, don''t leave bags unattended","dengue":"Year-round mosquito-borne risk (higher green season May–Nov); no widely available traveler vaccine — DEET/picaridin, cover at dawn/dusk, screened/AC rooms","water":"Tap water in San José & major tourist areas (incl. Manuel Antonio/Quepos) treated and generally safe; sensitive stomachs / remote lodges use bottled/filtered","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/costa-rica","read":"2026-08-20T14:54:18Z","page_updated":"2026-05-19T11:42:25+01:00","source_country":"costa-rica","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely"},"timing":{"inflection_curve_start":"late October–early November","peak":"mid-December–April (Christmas/New Year & Semana Santa ~1 yr lead)","fire_date":"2026-10-17","shoulder":"May–November (green-season value)","green":"May–November (afternoon rain; lush, lower rates)","booking_lead":"3–8 weeks normal peak; ~1 year for Christmas/New Year & Semana Santa (lead pressure on cliffside-resort + villa beds)","off_season_specials":"green-season resort/villa discounts + whale-watching backfill (Jul–Oct/Nov Southern-Hemisphere humpbacks)","event_peaks":["Whale season Jul–Oct/Nov (peak Aug–Sep)","Whale season Dec–Mar/Apr (peak Jan–Feb)","Christmas/New Year","Semana Santa (Easter)"],"operational_note":"Manuel Antonio NP closed every Tuesday — route park visit Wed–Mon; slot waterfalls/catamaran/mangrove on Tuesday"},"jewels":[{"name":"Playa Manuel Antonio (in-park)","si_tag":"Tropical Islands / Beaches","status":"live","hook":"Crescent white sand + calm turquoise — the park''s calmest, patrolled swim and best snorkel, backed by monkey-filled rainforest.","bookable_category":"guided park tour / DIY ticket","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.mustseespots.com/costa-rica/articles/manuel-antonio-national-park-beaches-wildlife-trails-explai