 superb family + wildlife half-day.","bookable_category":"half-day kayak tour","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.thecostaricatoursite.com/manuel-antonio/tours/Half-Day-Kayak-Damas-Mangroves.php + Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"expedition","blurb":"Calm-water estuary/mangrove kayak north of Quepos — monkeys, crocodiles and birds; superb family + wildlife half-day.","commission":"GYG/Viator affiliate + local operator; host-IATA private","accessed":"2026-07-06","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition","tropical","wildlife"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"primary","tropical":"evidenced","wildlife":"evidenced"},"commission_lane":["operator","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Rainmaker canopy + hanging bridges","si_tag":"GEA","status":"live","hook":"~1,400-acre private rainforest reserve with waterfalls, trails and Mistico-style suspension bridges — lower-crowd canopy near Manuel Antonio.","bookable_category":"guided canopy/bridges tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.earthtrekkers.com/things-to-do-in-manuel-antonio/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"expedition","blurb":"~1,400-acre private rainforest reserve with waterfalls, trails and Mistico-style suspension bridges — lower-crowd canopy near Manuel Antonio.","when":"year-round","commission":"GYG/Viator affiliate; host-IATA land services","accessed":"2026-07-06","wells":["stay","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"primary","tropical":"destination","wildlife":"destination"},"commission_lane":["affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Quepos marina sportfishing","si_tag":"GEA","status":"live","hook":"Marina Pez Vela — top Pacific billfish/sailfish + dorado sportfishing base; premier half/full-day charters.","bookable_category":"charter","tier":"premier","source":"https://costaricaexperts.com/destinations/manuel-antonio/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"mid-December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","blurb":"Marina Pez Vela — top Pacific billfish/sailfish + dorado sportfishing base; premier half/full-day charters.","when":"mid-December–April","commission":"host-IATA / private-charter agent-of-record; premium day rates","accessed":"2026-07-06","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"primary","tropical":"destination","wildlife":"destination"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"Whale-watching (Marino Ballena / Uvita)","si_tag":"GEA","status":"live","hook":"~45–60 min south; two humpback seasons (Jul–Oct/Nov + Dec–Mar/Apr) at the whale''s-tail sandbar — spans both green & dry season.","bookable_category":"guided whale-watching boat tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://puravidamoms.com/whale-watching-uvita-tour-guide/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"expedition","blurb":"~45–60 min south; two humpback seasons (Jul–Oct/Nov + Dec–Mar/Apr) at the whale''s-tail sandbar — spans both green & dry season.","commission":"GYG/Viator affiliate + host-IATA; Marino Ballena entry non-commissionable","accessed":"2026-07-06","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition","wildlife"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"primary","tropical":"destination","wildlife":"evidenced"},"commission_lane":["affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"National Park wildlife walk (sloths + 4 monkey species)","si_tag":"Wildlife","status":"future","hook":"2- & 3-toed sloths, capuchins, endangered squirrel monkeys, howlers, coatis, toucans — reliably seen with a certified scope-guide.","bookable_category":"guided park wildlife tour","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.adventuretourscostarica.com/blog/spotting-sloths-monkeys-your-manuel-antonio-wildlife-guide + Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"mid-December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"wildlife","blurb":"2- & 3-toed sloths, capuchins, endangered squirrel monkeys, howlers, coatis, toucans — reliably seen with a certified scope-guide.","when":"mid-December–April","commission":"GYG/Viator affiliate or host-IATA guide; park entry non-commissionable","accessed":"2026-07-06","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["wildlife"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"destination","tropical":"destination","wildlife":"primary"},"commission_lane":["affiliate","guide"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Manuel Antonio National Park open on Tuesday?","a":"No — the park is closed every Tuesday, year-round including holidays. It is open Wednesday–Monday 07:00–16:00; adult entry is $18, children 2–12 $5, under-2 free, and advance online ticket purchase with your passport number is required — route the park visit Wed–Mon.","source":"machupicchu.org, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Can you see whales near Manuel Antonio?","a":"Yes — nearby Marino Ballena / Uvita has two humpback seasons. Southern-Hemisphere humpbacks run Jul–Oct/Nov (peak Aug–Sep) and Northern-Hemisphere humpbacks Dec–Mar/Apr (peak Jan–Feb), a rare draw spanning both the green and dry seasons, ~45–60 min south by guided boat tour.","source":"puravidamoms.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is Manuel Antonio good for a honeymoon?","a":"Yes — it''s one of Costa Rica''s premier romance hubs. The cliffside-resort belt above the beach, led by adults-only Makanda by the Sea ~100 m above the ocean, defines the honeymoon identity, while Arenas del Mar is the only true beachfront luxury resort with two private beaches.","source":"oyster.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can you really see sloths and monkeys at the beach?","a":"Yes — it''s one of very few places anywhere you reliably can. Two- and three-toed sloths, white-faced capuchins (on 90%+ of visits), the endangered Central American squirrel monkey, howlers, coatis and toucans all live inside a compact, walkable national park where the rainforest meets the sand.","source":"adventuretourscostarica.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"wildlife-—-future"},{"q":"What''s the biggest safety risk in Manuel Antonio?","a":"Pacific rip currents — the leading cause of tourist drowning in Costa Rica (over 80% of drownings), on mostly unguarded beaches. Swim only at guarded/flagged beaches — the guarded park cove of Playa Manuel Antonio is the calmest water and the only patrolled swim — heed red flags, never swim alone, and if caught, swim parallel to shore.","source":"crie.cr, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Are the monkeys a problem in the park?","a":"They can be — capuchins, raccoons and coatis are bold and habituated and will raid open bags and grab food. Don''t feed wildlife, keep food sealed and bags zipped, and don''t leave belongings unattended on the beach.","source":"adventuretourscostarica.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Manuel Antonio, Costa Rica Travel Guide — Sloths, Rainforest Beaches, Cliffside Resorts & Quepos | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"See sloths and monkeys at a Pacific beach, base on the Quepos cliffs for romance or in a villa for family, and do Manuel Antonio well, safely, and at the right time — park hours, riptide safety, whales, catamarans and waterfalls.","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-06","search_language":"es-CR","local_keywords":["Parque Nacional Manuel Antonio","playas Manuel Antonio","qué hacer en Quepos","avistamiento de ballenas Uvita Marino Ballena","cataratas Nauyaca desde Manuel Antonio","kayak manglares isla Damas","perezosos y monos Manuel Antonio","hoteles de lujo Manuel Antonio","vuelo San José a Quepos","horario Parque Nacional Manuel Antonio precio entrada"],"hreflang":["en","es-CR"],"attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-07-06","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/costa-rica","read":"2026-08-20T14:54:18Z","source_updated":"2026-05-19T11:42:25+01:00"}]},"long_tail":["Manuel Antonio National Park hours 2026","is Manuel Antonio open on Tuesday","best time to visit Manuel Antonio Costa Rica","Manuel Antonio sloths and monkeys guide","Manuel Antonio riptide beach safety","SJO to Quepos flight Manuel Antonio","Manuel Antonio cliffside honeymoon resorts","Manuel Antonio villas with pool family","Nauyaca Waterfalls day trip from Manuel Antonio","Uvita whale watching season from Manuel Antonio"]},"booking":{"advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"tropical","status":"live"},{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"wildlife","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Arenas del Mar (Böÿ Collection / Cayuga)","why_ultra":"The only true beachfront luxury resort in Manuel Antonio — private ridge, two secluded beaches (golf-cart access), rainforest all around, strong sustainability, ocean-view suites with plunge pools. The apex property.","earning":"consortia/agent rate + amenity block; agent-of-record commission","consortia_value_add":"upgrade, breakfast/resort credit, early/late, VIP welcome (confirm current program)","mor":"Fora / host-IATA agent-of-record","tier":"luxury / ultra"},{"name":"Makanda by the Sea","why_ultra":"Adults-only (16+), ~100 m above the ocean on 12 acres of rainforest gardens — the definitive Manuel Antonio honeymoon/romance property; small, private, view-forward.","earning":"consortia/agent rate + amenity","consortia_value_add":"upgrade/credit where program allows (verify)","mor":"Fora / host-IATA","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Gaia Hotel & Reserve","why_ultra":"Eco-chic adults-oriented 22-room private-reserve hillside hotel; 500-thread-count linens, wellness + service focus.","earning":"consortia/agent rate","consortia_value_add":"upgrade/credit (verify)","mor":"Fora / host-IATA","tier":"premier / luxury"},{"name":"Tulemar Resort (+ private villas)","why_ultra":"Gated hillside estate with its own private sandy beach, 4 pools, concierge, spa, and a portfolio of private villas — the best resort-serviced villa play for families/multi-gen.","earning":"consortia/agent rate + villa MoR","consortia_value_add":"upgrade/credit + villa perks (verify)","mor":"Fora / host-IATA agent-of-record + villa direct-contract","tier":"premier / luxury (villas: luxury/ultra)"},{"name":"Preferred / luxury hillside villas","why_ultra":"Private ocean-view villas (chef/staff, pools, 2–8 br) — the whole-property-buyout ultra lane for honeymooners + multi-gen groups.","earning":"villa MoR + agent-of-record","consortia_value_add":"n/a (villa direct-contract perks vary)","mor":"direct-contract / villa specialist (host-IATA)","tier":"luxury / ultra"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"Manuel Antonio, Costa Rica"},"geo":{"lat":9.392,"lng":-84.137},"orbit":[{"id":"guanacaste-costa-rica","jewels":10,"si":["tropical","expedition","liveaboard","wellness","wildlife"]},{"id":"la-fortuna-arenal-costa-rica","jewels":10,"si":["expedition","romance","wellness"]},{"id":"monteverde-costa-rica","jewels":12,"si":["expedition","wildlife","romance"]},{"id":"nosara-costa-rica","jewels":10,"si":["tropical","expedition","wellness"]},{"id":"osa-peninsula-corcovado-costa-rica","jewels":9,"si":["expedition","diveglobal"]},{"id":"puerto-viejo-costa-rica","jewels":10,"si":["tropical","expedition","culture","wildlife","ocean"]},{"id":"san-jose-costa-rica","jewels":13,"si":["culture","expedition"]},{"id":"tortuguero-costa-rica","jewels":6,"si":["expedition","river"]}],"orbit_country":[]}'::jsonb, 64),
  ('mazamitla-mexico', '10S', 'Mazamitla', 'Mexico', 'Chalet cabañas in a pine-oak Sierra', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Jalisco (Puerto Vallarta & Guadalajara)', '{"expedition","family","adventure"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Pueblo Mágico (2005) at ~2,200 m in southern Jalisco, ~124–135 km / ~2 hr from Guadalajara; ''Switzerland of Mexico'' (Source: travelagewest.com, Accessed 2026-07-04)","Cool year-round (~15°C avg; ~7–26°C) — a magnet for Guadalajara residents, esp. summer (Source: en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mazamitla, Accessed 2026-07-04)","El Salto waterfall ~35 m in Los Cazos (private, ~US$1, ~45-min forest hike or horse ~M$250) (Source: zonaturistica.com, Accessed 2026-07-04)","Signature chalet cabañas (e.g., Cabañas Monteverde: kitchens, fireplaces, daily firewood) (Source: travelagewest.com, Accessed 2026-07-04)","Canopy/zipline + six-hanging-bridge tours (Green Forest Tours); La Zanja 1977 town forest (Source: theguadalajarapost.com, Accessed 2026-07-04)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"No major trauma hospital in town; nearest full ER/trauma is Guadalajara ~2 hr / ~124–135 km back down mountain road; local clinic for minor cases; air-evac to US for critical cases","book_enabled":false,"air_access_verified":"via GDL ~2 hr ground (not into a carve-out); approach via Hwy 405 (advisory-designated route)","advisory_note":"Advisory names Mazamitla as a specific EXCEPTION to the Hwy-110 restriction and directs ''travel via Highway 405 only'' — stronger than a blanket exclusion, but still NOT a named safe-zone carve-out; ruling holds at no-Book","malaria":"none","dengue":"very low at ~2,200 m (above Aedes aegypti elevation ceiling)","yellow_fever":"not required","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-20T14:49:02Z","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00","source_country":"mexico","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"consent","notes":"FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima.","fcdo_zones":[{"name":"The city of Tijuana, in Baja California","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["airside transit through Tijuana airport","the Cross Border Xpress bridge linking the airport across the border","federal toll road 1D and the Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border"]},{"name":"The city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"The state of Chihuahua","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Chihuahua","the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez via federal toll road 45","federal toll road 45D between Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez","the Copper Canyon rail route and the towns immediately on it, including Creel","the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro","state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua"],"note":"The advisory also covers the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"name":"The state of Sinaloa","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán","road 32 between El Fuerte and Los Mochis","the 15D federal toll road running the length of the state","the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis and El Fuerte, and the towns immediately on it"]},{"name":"The state of Tamaulipas","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo via federal toll road 85D from Monterrey","federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad Victoria and Magueyes","the area of Tamaulipas south of those highways"]},{"name":"The state of Zacatecas","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"In Guanajuato: the areas south-west of road 45D","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D. (San Miguel de Allende and Guanajuato City sit outside this area.)"},{"name":"The state of Michoacán","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Morelia via federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43","toll road 48D between Morelia and its airport","the town of Pátzcuaro via toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips on Lake Pátzcuaro","Federal Highway 15D"]},{"name":"In Jalisco: the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the Colima border","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Thirty-nine named municipalities, including Autlán de Navarro, Sayula, Tapalpa, Cocula and Villa Corona — the advisory lists each by name."},{"name":"In Jalisco: eleven northern municipalities","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Bolaños, Chimaltitán, Colotlán, Hostotipaquillo, Huejúcar, Huequilla el Alto, Mezquitic, San Martín de Bolaños, Santa María de los Ángeles, Totatiche and Villa Guerrero."},{"name":"The state of Colima","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Manzanillo by sea, or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport","direct travel via road 200 from that airport to Manzanillo"]},{"name":"The state of Guerrero, including the city of Acapulco","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air"]},{"name":"Within 40km of the Guatemalan border, from the Pacific Coast up to and including the Gracias a Dios crossing","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"Federal Highway 199 between Rancho Nuevo, outside San Cristóbal de las Casas, and the Chancalá junction outside Palenque","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"The restriction is the highway segment, not the towns at either end."}],"fcdo_zones_provenance":{"file":"src/data/safety.json","ref":"f8666636bc25790e0c9643ad5656f8d9fea37bf6","ref_committed":"2026-08-30T05:44:55Z","country_iso2":"MX","summary":"The FCDO advises against all but essential travel to named states, cities and border areas of Mexico — listed below in its own words, each with its own exceptions. The Yucatán Peninsula, Mexico City, Baja California Sur and the other main visitor regions carry no FCDO restriction.","source":"UK FCDO — Mexico travel advice, reviewed 2026-07-16 (verbatim snapshot from the research library)","_rule":"the FCDO restricted-area records for this country, verbatim. PRESENCE OF THIS BLOCK IS NOT A CLAIM THAT THIS DESTINATION SITS IN ANY OF THEM — membership is a coverage judgement and is set only in `zone_record`, by a human."}},"timing":{"peak":"Domestic-holiday & weekend peaks — summer (GDL heat escape) + Semana Santa + Christmas/New-Year + long weekends; cool ~15°C year-round draw","waterfall_flow_peak":"October–December (fullest El Salto flow, post-rains)","shoulder":"Non-holiday weekdays / shoulder months","green":"Deep off-holiday midweeks (softest domestic demand)","booking_lead":"Weeks–months for Semana Santa/summer/Christmas/long-weekend cabañas; midweek walk-up-easy; largely direct/domestic","event_peaks":"Semana Santa, summer school holidays, Christmas–New-Year, Mexican puentes","fire_date":"''Cool-mountain weekend from Guadalajara'' ahead of summer + Semana Santa; waterfall-flow (Oct–Dec) into fall"},"jewels":[{"name":"El Salto waterfall (Los Cazos)","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"future","hook":"~35 m waterfall, ~45-min forest hike (or horseback) to a wooden overlook","bookable_category":"site entry (~US$1) + guide/horse","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.zonaturistica.com/en/things-to-do/jalisco/mazamitla/the-salto-waterfall (Accessed 2026-07-04)","si":"expedition","blurb":"~35 m waterfall, ~45-min forest hike (or horseback) to a wooden overlook","commission":"day-tour or curated-recommend","accessed":"2026-07-04","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","expedition":"primary","family":"destination"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"La Zanja town forest","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"future","hook":"1977 municipal pine forest — trails, cabins, rentable grills","bookable_category":"free/low-cost","tier":"essential","source":"https://theguadalajarapost.com/2022/06/03/mazamitla-jalisco-what-to-do-and-how-to-get-to-this-magical-town/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","si":"expedition","blurb":"1977 municipal pine forest — trails, cabins, rentable grills","commission":"curated-recommend","accessed":"2026-07-04","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","expedition":"primary","family":"destination"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"Canopy + six hanging bridges (Green Forest Tours)","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"future","hook":"3-hr zipline + 2-hr six-hanging-bridge forest walk","bookable_category":"operator","tier":"comfort","source":"https://theguadalajarapost.com/2022/06/03/mazamitla-jalisco-what-to-do-and-how-to-get-to-this-magical-town/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"expedition","blurb":"3-hr zipline + 2-hr six-hanging-bridge forest walk","when":"year-round","commission":"activity affiliate / day-tour","accessed":"2026-07-04","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["adventure","expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"evidenced","expedition":"primary","family":"destination"},"commission_lane":["affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Chalet cabañas (Cabañas Monteverde)","si_tag":"Family","status":"future","hook":"Wooden chalet cabins with kitchens + fireplaces (daily firewood) — the definitive stay","bookable_category":"direct (domestic)","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.travelagewest.com/Travel/Mexico/mazamitla-mexico-travel-guide (Accessed 2026-07-04)","si":"family","blurb":"Wooden chalet cabins with kitchens + fireplaces (daily firewood) — the definitive stay","commission":"curated-recommend (direct-only)","accessed":"2026-07-04","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["family"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","expedition":"destination","family":"primary"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"Enchanted Garden (Los Cazos)","si_tag":"Family","status":"future","hook":"Greenery + crystalline stream, toured on foot/bike/horseback/ATV","bookable_category":"site entry + rentals","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.travelagewest.com/Travel/Mexico/mazamitla-mexico-travel-guide (Accessed 2026-07-04)","si":"family","blurb":"Greenery + crystalline stream, toured on foot/bike/horseback/ATV","commission":"day-tour / curated","accessed":"2026-07-04","wells":["gear"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["family"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","expedition":"destination","family":"primary"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"Los Cazos ATV + horseback","si_tag":"Adventure / Ecotourism","status":"future","hook":"ATV tours + horse rides through pine-oak forest","bookable_category":"licensed operator","tier":"comfort","source":"https://theguadalajarapost.com/2022/06/03/mazamitla-jalisco-what-to-do-and-how-to-get-to-this-magical-town/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","si":"adventure","blurb":"ATV tours + horse rides through pine-oak forest","commission":"activity affiliate / day-tour","accessed":"2026-07-04","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["Adventure / Ecotourism","adventure"],"shelf_fit":{"Adventure / Ecotourism":"evidenced","adventure":"primary","expedition":"destination","family":"destination"},"commission_lane":["affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane","si_raw":"Adventure / Ecotourism","si_map_basis":"normalised from free text ''Adventure / Ecotourism'' by gen_normalise_jewel_si"}],"faq":[{"q":"Can I book a stay in Mazamitla through TravelWell?","a":"No — it is content-only, recommended only as a licensed day/weekend trip from the Guadalajara carve-out. notably, though, the advisory names Mazamitla as an exception to the Highway 110 restriction and permits access \"via Highway 405 only.\" book_enabled=FALSE.","source":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"The ~2-hour mountain road transfer, not the town''s street crime (which is low — a domestic family town). The drive from Guadalajara leaves the GDL safe zone, even on the advisory-approved Highway 405, which is the hold reason; use licensed daytime transport only, and note the nearest full trauma hospital is ~2 hr back in Guadalajara.","source":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What is there to do at El Salto waterfall?","a":"Hike to it. The ~35 m El Salto falls in Los Cazos are reached by a ~45-minute forest trail (or a horse, ~M$250) to a wooden overlook, entry ~US$1, with the fullest flow October–December after the rains. Sturdy footwear, and turn back in weather.","source":"zonaturistica.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is Mazamitla good for a family weekend?","a":"Yes — it is the classic Guadalajara family escape. The product is a wooden chalet cabaña with a full kitchen and fireplace (Cabañas Monteverde delivers firewood daily) in a cool ~15°C pine-oak Pueblo Mágico at 2,200 m; cabañas sell out for Semana Santa, summer and Christmas, so book weeks to months ahead.","source":"travelagewest.com / en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"family"},{"q":"What adventure activities are on offer?","a":"Zip, ride and cross bridges. Green Forest Tours runs a 3-hour zipline and a 2-hour six-hanging-bridge walk, plus ATV, horseback and mountain-biking through the forest and Los Cazos. Use licensed operators with helmet/harness checks — evac to Guadalajara is ~2 hr, so injuries carry a distance penalty.","source":"theguadalajarapost.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"adventure"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Mazamitla Travel Guide — Jalisco''s ''Mexican Switzerland'' Cabaña Mountain Pueblo Mágico | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Jalisco''s cool pine-forest Pueblo Mágico at 2,200 m — chalet cabañas, the El Salto waterfall, canopy tours, and straight guidance: an interior day/weekend trip from Guadalajara (Hwy 405), not a bookable base.","slug":"mazamitla-mexico","primary_keyword":"Mazamitla Mexico travel guide","long_tail":["Mazamitla from Guadalajara day trip","El Salto waterfall Mazamitla","Mazamitla cabañas Monteverde","is Mazamitla safe","Mazamitla Suiza Mexicana things to do"],"search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Mazamitla Pueblo Mágico","Mazamitla desde Guadalajara","cascada El Salto Mazamitla","cabañas en Mazamitla","Mazamitla la Suiza Mexicana","tirolesa puentes colgantes Mazamitla"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-04","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-07-04","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-20T14:49:02Z","source_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}]}},"booking":{"advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"expedition","status":"future"},{"si":"family","status":"future"},{"si":"Adventure / Ecotourism","status":"future"}],"ultra":[],"source_verified":"