m/hot-springs-mendoza-cacheuta-thermal-baths/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"natural Andean hot springs on the Mendoza River, multi-temperature stone pools, Argentina''s only grotto sauna, mud baths, and a Creole asado buffet","si":"romance","blurb":"natural Andean hot springs on the Mendoza River, multi-temperature stone pools, Argentina''s only grotto sauna, mud baths, and a Creole asado buffet","when":"year-round","commission":"affiliate spa day 4–8% / DMC","wells":["activities","beauty","eat"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["romance","romance+wellness","wellness"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","expedition":"destination","romance":"primary","romance+wellness":"evidenced","wellness":"evidenced"},"commission_pct_low":4,"commission_pct_high":8,"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane","si_raw":"romance+wellness","si_map_basis":"normalised from free text ''romance+wellness'' by gen_normalise_jewel_si"},{"name":"Alta Montaña + Aconcagua viewpoint + Puente del Inca","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.getyourguide.com/mendoza-l673/andes-day-trip-uspallata-aconcagua-and-puente-del-inca-t55889/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"Route 7 full-day: Potrerillos Dam, Uspallata, Puente del Inca''s natural stone-and-hot-spring formation, and the Aconcagua Provincial Park viewpoint of the 6,961 m peak","si":"expedition","blurb":"Route 7 full-day: Potrerillos Dam, Uspallata, Puente del Inca''s natural stone-and-hot-spring formation, and the Aconcagua Provincial Park viewpoint of the 6,961 m peak","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC / affiliate day 4–20%","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","expedition":"primary","romance":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":4,"commission_pct_high":20,"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Mendoza River rafting (Potrerillos)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://solsalute.com/blog/adventure-tourism-in-potrerillos-mendoza/","timing":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Class II–IV depending on season/flow; certified rescue guides, kayak support, and full safety kit standard. Guided: mandatory — never run this river unguided","si":"expedition","blurb":"Class II–IV depending on season/flow; certified rescue guides, kayak support, and full safety kit standard. Guided: mandatory — never run this river unguided","when":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","commission":"affiliate / DMC 4–15%","wells":["activities","gear"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","expedition":"primary","romance":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":4,"commission_pct_high":15,"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Uspallata & the high desert","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.myguideargentina.com/experiences/mendoza-uspallata-aconcagua-and-puente-del-inca-day-trip","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"cinematic Andean valley, gateway between the wine plain and the summit corridor; horseback and 4x4 add-ons","si":"expedition","blurb":"cinematic Andean valley, gateway between the wine plain and the summit corridor; horseback and 4x4 add-ons","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC day 10–20%","wells":["activities","move"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","expedition":"primary","romance":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":20,"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"Why is Mendoza the world''s Malbec capital?","a":"Because the concentration is unmatched: Argentina holds roughly 75% of the world''s Malbec vines, and about 75% of Argentina''s vineyards lie in Mendoza — making it the single most important place on the planet for the grape and the global epicenter of Malbec.","source":"winefolly.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Mendoza?","a":"Late February through April — harvest and the Fiesta Nacional de la Vendimia (2026 central acts Mar 6–10) — is the most atmospheric window. Spring (Oct–Nov) is the value-and-balance alternative, with rates running ~15–25% below harvest peaks; either way, book icon wineries and lodges 3–4 months ahead of the Feb–April peak.","source":"across-southamerica.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"Which honeymoon wine-lodge should we book?","a":"The two ultra beds are Awasi Mendoza (Relais & Châteaux, Luján de Cuyo, 18 adobe rooms/villas on a ~60-acre private vineyard) and The Vines Resort & Spa (Valle de Uco, 21 private villas across 1,500 acres with vine-side dining). Both commission best through luxury consortia (Virtuoso/Fora), typically ~10%+ plus amenities.","source":"scottdunn.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can you see Aconcagua on a day trip from Mendoza?","a":"Yes. Route 7 climbs the Alta Montaña corridor past Potrerillos (1,350 m), Uspallata (1,900 m), and Puente del Inca (2,720 m) to the Aconcagua Provincial Park viewpoint of the 6,961 m peak, the highest in the Western Hemisphere. The day-trip tops out ~2,700 m (mild breathlessness possible); Aconcagua summit mountaineering is a separate, expedition-grade activity requiring permits and licensed guides.","source":"getyourguide.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Mendoza?","a":"Drink-driving. Wine touring plus self-drive is the single most important avoidable risk, so the standard doctrine is always a designated driver or a guided wine tour with transport — never self-drive between tastings, and ride sober on the Maipú bike-and-wine route.","source":"machupicchu.org, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is Mendoza River rafting dangerous?","a":"Guided, it is a managed risk. Rafting at Potrerillos runs Class II–III, up to Class IV in high summer flow, with certified rescue guides, kayak safety support, and full neoprene/helmet/PFD standard — book certified operators only, and never run the river unguided.","source":"solsalute.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Mendoza & Argentina Wine Country — Malbec, Valle de Uco & the Andes | TravelWell","search_language":"es-AR","local_keywords":["bodegas Mendoza","Valle de Uco vinos","Ruta del Vino Mendoza","Vendimia","Alta Montaña Aconcagua","termas de Cacheuta","Malbec de altura"],"hreflang":["en","es-AR"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-08-20","last_verified_basis":"safety.fcdo.read","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/argentina","read":"2026-08-20T14:54:24Z","source_updated":"2026-05-07T17:26:11+01:00"}]},"content_freshness":"2026-07-07"},"booking":{"advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"name":"Awasi Mendoza (formerly Cavas Wine Lodge)","brand":"Relais & Châteaux","area":"Luján de Cuyo","product":"18 adobe rooms/villas on ~60-acre private vineyard","earning":"Virtuoso/Fora consortia commission + amenities; MoR via consortium/DMC","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"The Vines Resort & Spa","area":"Valle de Uco","product":"21 