ee-room cycle","si":"culture","blurb":"best-preserved Classic Maya murals on Earth, full-color three-room cycle","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"full-day DMC tour","wells":["activities","stay"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary","expedition":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Yaxchilán by Usumacinta riverboat","si_tag":"culture","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Palenque/Tour-Bonampak-and-Yaxchilan/d23479-30922P9","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Usumacinta motorboat into the Lacandón, ruins the road cannot reach","si":"culture","blurb":"Usumacinta motorboat into the Lacandón, ruins the road cannot reach","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"licensed river-tour DMC (border-verify)","wells":["move","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary","expedition":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Agua Azul cascades","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Palenque/Agua-Azul-and-Misol-Ha/d23479-30922P10","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"waterfall day-tour affiliate","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","expedition":"primary"},"commission_lane":["affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Misol-Ha waterfall (Predator site)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/things-to-do-in-palenque/","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"day-tour affiliate","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","expedition":"primary"},"commission_lane":["affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Roberto Barrios cascades","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://nomadearthcatalog.com/cascadas-roberto-barrios/","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"five off-the-beaten-track falls, turquoise pools, natural 10 m slide, ~45 min south, entry ~30 MXN","si":"expedition","blurb":"five off-the-beaten-track falls, turquoise pools, natural 10 m slide, ~45 min south, entry ~30 MXN","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"dedicated day-tour affiliate","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","expedition":"primary"},"commission_lane":["affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Howler-monkey jungle canopy (dawn ruins)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.timetravelturtle.com/mexico/visit-palenque/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"the sound that defines dawn at Palenque; the ruins double as a wildlife encounter","si":"expedition","blurb":"the sound that defines dawn at Palenque; the ruins double as a wildlife encounter","when":"year-round","commission":"guided dawn tour upsell","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture","expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"evidenced","expedition":"primary"},"commission_lane":["guide"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Lacandón Jungle multi-day expedition","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"premier","source":"https://mayantourstravel.com/tours/the-amazing-lacandon-jungle-groups/","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"deep-forest circuit combining Bonampak, Yaxchilán and river camps","si":"expedition","blurb":"deep-forest circuit combining Bonampak, Yaxchilán and river camps","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"multi-day DMC","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","expedition":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for — is the road dangerous?","a":"The road is the risk, not the ruins. The overland San Cristóbal↔Palenque highway via Ocosingo (Chilón) has a documented armed-robbery history — one reported incident had ~18 men with assault rifles set a roadblock and rob a line of tourist vehicles, with the worst incidents after dark. The rule is daytime-only, guided/convoy transfer, no self-drive, and the safer, longer Villahermosa toll-road approach where possible.","source":"mexiconewsdaily.com / jeniastraveldiaries.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"How remote is medical care from Palenque?","a":"Genuinely remote — plan for it. Palenque is a small town with limited advanced care; serious trauma routes to Villahermosa or Tuxtla Gutiérrez, with air evacuation to Mexico City for anything major. Bonampak, Yaxchilán and the deep-jungle waterfalls are hours from a hospital, so carry evacuation insurance — and note dengue is present year-round with malaria risk in rural Chiapas.","source":"mexiconewsdaily.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What will I see at the Palenque ruins?","a":"A Maya city the rainforest never fully released: the Temple of the Inscriptions rising over Pakal the Great''s tomb, and the four-story observation tower of the Palace, its civic heart. The tomb chamber itself has been closed to descent since ~2004 to protect it, so you see the pyramid and Pakal''s regalia at the site museum, not the crypt. Go at the 8 AM opening before the jungle heat.","source":"mayaruins.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What are the Palenque waterfalls, and when should I go?","a":"Three systems within reach: Agua Azul''s 500+ turquoise cascades over ~6 km, the ~35 m Misol-Ha plunge with a walk-behind grotto, and the quieter Roberto Barrios falls with a natural rock slide (~45 min south, entry ~30 MXN). Come November–April, when the mineral-rich water runs brilliant turquoise; in the May–October rains sediment turns Agua Azul brown. Swim only in marked zones — currents are strong.","source":"mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Can I visit Bonampak and Yaxchilán?","a":"Yes, as a full-day guided expedition. Bonampak holds the best-preserved Classic Maya murals in existence (~792 AD), and Yaxchilán is reachable only by motorboat on the Usumacinta River, the water border with Guatemala. Go with a licensed operator, not an ad-hoc boatman, verify current border and security conditions before booking, and travel by daylight with life vests.","source":"viator.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Palenque, Mexico: Jungle Maya Ruins, Waterfalls & Safe Travel Guide (2026) | TravelWell","search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["ruinas de Palenque","Agua Azul Chiapas","Misol-Ha","Yaxchilán Bonampak","cascadas Roberto Barrios","Templo de las Inscripciones Pakal","cómo llegar a Palenque desde Villahermosa"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","primary_keyword":"Palenque","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-08-20","last_verified_basis":"safety.fcdo.read","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-20T14:49:02Z","source_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}]},"content_freshness":"2026-07-07"},"booking":{"advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","status":"live"},{"si":"expedition","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Chan-Kah Resort Village","tier":"premier","mor":"bedbank/direct","earning":"modest — upper-mid ADR, not luxury; live"},{"name":"Boutique Quinta Chanabnal","tier":"premier","mor":"advisor/direct","earning":"modest"},{"name":"Piedra de Agua Palenque","tier":"comfort","mor":"verify","earning":"to verify"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Palenque, Mexico, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":17.484,"lng":-92.046},"orbit":[{"id":"san-cristobal-de-las-casas-mexico","jewels":10,"si":["culture"]}],"orbit_country":["akumal-mexico","bacalar-mexico","balandra-beach-mexico","cabo-pulmo-mexico","cabo-san-lucas-mexico","calakmul-mexico","campeche-city-mexico","cancun-mexico","careyes-mexico","celestun-mexico","chapala-ajijic-mexico","chichen-itza-mexico","coba-mexico","costalegre-mexico","cozumel-mexico","east-cape-mexico","ensenada-mexico","espiritu-santo-island-mexico","guadalajara-mexico","guanajuato-city-mexico","holbox-mexico","huatulco-mexico","isla-contoy-mexico","isla-mujeres-mexico","izamal-mexico","la-paz-mexico","loreto-mexico","los-barriles-mexico","magdalena-bay-mexico","mahahual-mexico","mazamitla-mexico","merida-mexico","mexico-city-mexico","oaxaca-city-mexico","playa-del-carmen-mexico","puerto-aventuras-mexico","puerto-morelos-mexico","puerto-vallarta-mexico","punta-mita-mexico","rio-lagartos-mexico","san-jose-del-cabo-mexico","san-miguel-de-allende-mexico","san-sebastian-del-oeste-mexico","sayulita-mexico","sian-kaan-mexico","teotihuacan-mexico","tlaquepaque-mexico","todos-santos-mexico","tulum-mexico","uxmal-mexico","valladolid-mexico","valle-de-guadalupe-mexico","puerto-escondido-mexico"]}'::jsonb, 76),
  ('pantanal-brazil', '10S', 'The Pantanal, Brazil', 'Brazil', 'The Pantanal', 'live', 'verified', 'safariJeep', 'Amazon, Pantanal & Iguaçu', '{"safari","wildlife","expedition"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"190","emergency_secondary":["193 fire/environmental","192 SAMU medical"],"advisory_note":"route to the park","book_enabled":true,"air_access_verified":true,"air_access":{"north":"CGB (Cuiabá) — Porto Jofre / Transpantaneira","south":"CGR (Campo Grande) — Caiman / Southern reserves"},"remote_flag":true,"medevac_note":"hours by dirt road + river to trauma care (Cuiabá north / Campo Grande south); comprehensive insurance w/ medical evacuation is a standard attach","health":{"malaria":"low; zone-dependent (present in parts of state of Mato Grosso / Northern; NOT in Cuiabá city nor Mato Grosso do Sul / Southern)","dengue_chikungunya":"flag — present; insect protection regardless of malaria zone","yellow_fever":"vaccination recommended for Mato Grosso"},"wildlife_water_rules":["life vests on all boat safaris","no-approach / minimum-distance on jaguars","no swimming in caiman/piranha waters","stay in vehicle/boat","no feeding or baiting"],"fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/brazil","read":"2026-08-20T14:54:23Z","page_updated":"2026-05-11T12:32:48+01:00","source_country":"brazil","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely","fcdo_zones":[{"name":"River areas in the west of Amazonas State","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Along the Amazon River and its tributaries west of Codajás and east of Belém do Solimões; any part of the Itaquaí River; any part of the Japurá River or its tributaries; and the Rio Negro and its tributaries north or west of Barcelos."}],"fcdo_zones_provenance":{"file":"src/data/safety.json","ref":"f8666636bc25790e0c9643a